<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Coast2Kosci_2026_Database" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata><name>Coast to Kosci (C2K) 2026 Official Course &amp; Waypoints</name></metadata>
  <wpt lat="-37.092035" lon="149.872274"><ele>7</ele><name>0.0km - Boydtown Beach Start Line (Twofold Bay)</name><desc>Start | Fri 05:30 (Race Start) | Toilets: STRICTLY NO TOILETS - PENALTIES APPLY | Nearest 24h toilet before start is Quarantine Bay (~2 km) or Eden (~4 km). Bushes strictly prohibited.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.090589" lon="149.868690"><ele>8</ele><name>0.5km - Nullica River Bridge &amp; Princes Hwy Crossing (0.5-0.7 km)</name><desc>Mandatory Road Crossing / Hazard |  | Toilets: None | Marshal Crossing #1 (Bega Valley). Penalties apply for ignoring crossing officials.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.089905" lon="149.843209"><ele>95</ele><name>3.7km - Aid Station #1 (Brandy Creek Trail / Nullica Rd &amp; Towamba Rd)</name><desc>Official Race Aid Station + Road Crossing |  | Toilets: None | Marshal Crossing #2. Crew vehicles turn left from Princes Hwy into Towamba Rd and proceed straight to CP1 Towamba.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.081583" lon="149.694362"><ele>38</ele><name>24.4km - CP 1 Towamba (Towamba Rd &amp; Pericoe Rd) + School BBQ &amp; Hall Toilets</name><desc>Official Checkpoint + Community Aid + Toilet |  | Toilets: Public Toilets (Towamba Hall 24h ~690m; Sports fields ~1.2 km drive) | Marshal Crossing #3 at 23.9-24.4 km. Support Crew Chief texts C2K WhatsApp group upon clearance.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.006960" lon="149.619560"><ele>155</ele><name>36.6km - Wyndham / Towamba St -&gt; Big Jack Mountain Rd Junction</name><desc>Mandatory Road Crossing / Navigation Point |  | Toilets: Wyndham Hall 24h public toilet (~7.6 km detour off Big Jack Mtn Rd if crew detours) | Marathon point (42.18 km) passed shortly ahead along Big Jack Mountain Rd at ~169 m elevation.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.974480" lon="149.584152"><ele>169</ele><name>42.2km - Marathon Point (42.2 km Marker)</name><desc>Course Milestone |  | Toilets: None | Approx 100m past causeway on Big Jack Mountain Rd.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.927179" lon="149.503211"><ele>209</ele><name>51.7km - CP 2 Rocky Hall (Public Telephone, Restrooms &amp; Society Stall)</name><desc>Official Checkpoint + Community Aid + Toilet |  | Toilets: Public Toilets (Official Restrooms right at Rocky Hall CP2, 51.68 km) | Great toilet &amp; caffeine stop before climbing out of the coastal valley onto the Monaro tableland.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.897993" lon="149.463533"><ele>290</ele><name>57.2km - Base of Big Jack Mountain (Restroom &amp; Mandatory Pacer Climb Start)</name><desc>Toilet / Mandatory Pacer Safety Zone |  | Toilets: Public Toilet (Opposite side of road to the park) | Note: RWGPS &amp; updated Course Directions route via Cow Bail Trail (turn left 56.1 km, right 56.4 km) then rejoin towards Coolangubra Forest Way -&gt; Mt Darragh Rd (65.9 km Marshal Crossing #5).</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.843248" lon="149.391237"><ele>797</ele><name>69.7km - CP 3 Cathcart General Store &amp; Cut-Off #1 + Rest Area Toilets</name><desc>Official Checkpoint / Hard Cut-Off + Store + Toilet | Fri 20 Nov 17:30 AEDT | Toilets: Public Toilets (~200m past store at 69.87 km - Cathcart Rest Area, Daylight hours, Water + Shower) | Minimum cumulative speed required: 5.83 km/h (10:17 min/km).</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.838292" lon="149.310045"><ele>760</ele><name>77.4km - Black Lake Reserve Public Toilet (Bibbenluke Approach)</name><desc>Public Toilet (Corridor) |  | Toilets: Public Toilet (24 hours, 215m off course) | 3.6 km before entering Monaro Hwy.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.816199" lon="149.283011"><ele>733</ele><name>81.0km - Bibbenluke / Monaro Hwy (B23) &amp; Bombala River Bridge (81.0-81.6 km)</name><desc>Mandatory Road Crossing / Penalty Zone |  | Toilets: None | Marshal Crossing #6 at 81.6 km. Officials watch Bibbenluke closely and apply time penalties for running on the left.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.747355" lon="149.151747"><ele>761</ele><name>97.6km - Gunningrach Rd Right Fork &amp; Big Dead Tree Landmark (101.9 km)</name><desc>Navigation Hazard / Landmark |  | Toilets: None | Big Dead Tree landmark sits on the right on uphill at 101.93 km.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.690866" lon="149.159959"><ele>925</ele><name>106.6km - CP 4 Gunningrach Rd &amp; Snowy River Way (Cut-Off #2)</name><desc>Official Checkpoint / Hard Cut-Off + Pacer Gate | Fri 20 Nov 23:30 AEDT | Toilets: None | Minimum cumulative speed required: 5.93 km/h (10:07 min/km). Long 41.4 km night leg ahead to Dalgety.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.504090" lon="148.834251"><ele>756</ele><name>148.0km - CP 5 Dalgety Memorial Hall, Rear Toilets &amp; Dalgety Bridge Cut-Off #3</name><desc>Official Checkpoint / Hard Cut-Off + Community Soup + Toilet | Sat 21 Nov 06:30 AEDT (Dalgety Bridge West side 148.25 km) | Toilets: Hall Toilets = RUNNERS ONLY; Rear building 50-100m behind Hall (Brierly St) = Support Crew | Minimum cumulative speed required: 5.93 km/h (10:07 min/km). Public telephone landmark opposite Dalgety Pub.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.537240" lon="148.697510"><ele>959.0</ele><name>162.0km - Beloka Hill Ascent (162.0 - 165.0 km)</name><desc>Mandatory Pacer Safety Zone + No-Parking Climb |  | Toilets: None | Exact Beloka climb starts right after crossing Guises Creek (~161.9 km); steep exposed morning climb.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.413939" lon="148.609790"><ele>914</ele><name>181.7km - Jindabyne Roundabout Crossing &amp; Claypits Lake Path Toilets (181.7-181.9 km)</name><desc>Mandatory Road Crossing + 24h Toilet + Town Resupply |  | Toilets: Public Toilets (Claypits Foreshore Park 24h + Water, 11m off course; Kalkite St 24h; BP 6am-10pm; Town Centre CLOSED) | Check shop closing times (~7pm) if slower schedule puts you in Jindabyne after dark - actually Cut-off #4 is Sat 14:00 so all active runners clear before afternoon close.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.409587" lon="148.596930"><ele>924</ele><name>183.9km - CP 6 Jindabyne Caravan &amp; Holiday Discovery Park (Cut-Off #4)</name><desc>Official Checkpoint / Hard Cut-Off | Sat 21 Nov 14:00 AEDT | Toilets: Shell Jindabyne adjacent (6am-4pm); Caravan Park reception | Minimum cumulative speed required: 5.66 km/h (10:36 min/km). Long 38 km climb to Charlotte Pass begins after Jindabyne.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.369244" lon="148.589289"><ele>1030</ele><name>189.8km - Little Thredbo River Rest Area (Kosciuszko NP)</name><desc>Public Toilet (National Park) |  | Toilets: Public Toilet (24 hours, 69m off course) | Crosses Thredbo River vicinity before climbing Sawpit Creek.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.350217" lon="148.564040"><ele>1204</ele><name>195.5km - Sawpit Creek Rest Area (Kosciuszko NP)</name><desc>Public Toilet (National Park) |  | Toilets: Public Toilet (24 hours, 50m off course) | Key mountain climb milestone along Kosciuszko Rd.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.405495" lon="148.412360"><ele>1722</ele><name>213.1km - CP 7 Perisher Valley (Bus Shelter in front of Ski-Tube Station)</name><desc>Official Checkpoint |  | Toilets: No 24h public toilet confirmed on National Toilet Map | Last checkpoint before the Summit Path gear inspection at Charlotte Pass.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.431598" lon="148.328858"><ele>1838</ele><name>222.1km - CP 8 Charlotte Pass (Turnaround Loop Car Park &amp; Cut-Off #5)</name><desc>Official Checkpoint / Hard Cut-Off + Gear Inspection + Toilet | Sat 21 Nov 23:00 AEDT | Toilets: Public Toilet (Charlotte Pass Lookout 24h, 22m off course) | Minimum cumulative speed required: 5.35 km/h (11:13 min/km). Secure all crew food inside vehicles against ravens/currawongs.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.450278" lon="148.282633"><ele>2020</ele><name>228.1km - Seamans Hut (Summit Path Outbound &amp; 234.6 km Return)</name><desc>Alpine Emergency Shelter + 24h Toilet |  | Toilets: National Park 24h Toilet (adjacent to Seamans Hut) | Passed twice: ~228.06 km outbound and ~234.58 km return.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.457690" lon="148.268770"><ele>2122</ele><name>229.6km - Rawson Pass (Summit Path Outbound &amp; 232.9 km Return)</name><desc>Alpine Emergency Shelter + 24h Toilet |  | Toilets: National Park 24h Toilet (Australia's highest public toilets, 16m off course) | Passed twice: ~229.64 km outbound and ~232.90 km return.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.455849" lon="148.263550"><ele>2228</ele><name>231.3km - Mount Kosciuszko Summit (2,228 m Turnaround)</name><desc>Summit / Turnaround |  | Toilets: None (nearest Rawson Pass 1.6 km below) | 9.35 km remaining back down to Charlotte Pass Finish Line.</desc></wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.431729" lon="148.328413"><ele>1839</ele><name>240.7km - Charlotte Pass Finish Line (End of Summit Walk)</name><desc>Finish / Final Cut-Off | Sun 22 Nov 03:30 AEDT | Toilets: Public Toilet (Charlotte Pass Lookout 24h) | First-time finishers earn iconic Akubra hat; repeat finishers earn C2K hat pin; all receive 2026 finisher shirt.</desc></wpt>
  <trk><name>Coast To Kosci Ultramarathon 240.65 km</name><trkseg>
